From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: setup's choices keep their text clear of the check mark

On the setup screen that asks how to start (Full experience or Minimal),
the check mark of the chosen card covered the end of its text: the
screen's own padding for the cards (Chrome 0058) replaced the shared
card styles' padding on the sides too, whose end side leaves room for the
check mark. Only the cards' top and bottom padding is the screen's now.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/resources/chromeos/login/screens/common/nickel_setup.html b/chrome/browser/resources/chromeos/login/screens/common/nickel_setup.html
index 6a7ab47..c5ed0aa 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/resources/chromeos/login/screens/common/nickel_setup.html
+++ b/chrome/browser/resources/chromeos/login/screens/common/nickel_setup.html
@@ -15,8 +15,11 @@ found in the LICENSE file.
     margin-bottom: 12px;
   }
 
+  /* Only the cards' height is ours: their sides keep the shared styles'
+     padding, whose end side leaves room for the check mark. */
   .card-container {
-    padding: 12px 16px;
+    padding-bottom: 12px;
+    padding-top: 12px;
   }
 
   .nickel-setup-either-way {
